        "targetText": "1. Keep the actual spaces and construct the conditional residualReuse the SAME actual65 laws,normalized conditional kernel,reflection,root,inverse and polar witnesses. P is conditional expectation given Y. Idempotence gives P(g−Pg)=0, so the canonical bounded map R has exact codomain ker P; R is identity there.Rg=g−Pg∈ker⁡P,Ri⊥=Iker⁡P.Corresponding Lean step  classical\n  dsimp only\n  let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n  let J := (μ.prod (stdGaussian E)).map\n    (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2))\n  let ν := J.snd\n  let mY : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := MeasurableSpace.comap Prod.snd (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace E)\n  letI : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := Prod.instMeasurableSpace\n  letI : Fact (mY ≤ (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace (E × E))) := ⟨measurable_snd.coma",
