        "targetText": "5. Construct centered macroscopic input and its exact norm decompositionFor every globally centered f, selfadjoint conditional expectation and Pq_P=q_P give E[f|Y]∈H_P^0. Apply the ambient identity to Rf and its idempotence, then the SAME restricted-root relation. Orthogonal projection gives the Pythagorean norm identity.∫fdJ=0⇒fP∈HP0,B∗i⊥f⊥=i0Γ0fV=ΓPi0fV,‖f‖2=‖fP‖2+‖f⊥‖2.Corresponding Lean step  refine ⟨hμ,hJ,hν,hRange,hPf,S,hS,hSd,hSc,hSf,hSs,e,he,U,hU,hUi,hUs,T,hTs,hAll,\n    hAeq,hAs,hAn,hPB,Γ,hΓ,hΓSq,hΓP,hΓPSq,hGram,q,hqa,hTq,hq,hCenter,hΓPq,hγ,\n    ΓP0,hΓP0,hPos0,hOrder0,hUnit,Inv,hLeft,hRight,hNormInv,B0,hB0,V0,hVdef,\n    hFactor,hVadj,hVnorm,R,hR,hAmbient,?_⟩\n  intro f hf\n  have hCf : C f ∈ HP0 := by\n    change inner ℝ qP (C f)=0\n    change inner ℝ (qP : Lp ℝ 2 J) (P f)=0\n    rw [← ",
